        {
          "id": 1219615081,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "It *should* for `ui/qt/main.cpp` and `ui/logray/logray_main.cpp`, unless your top-level directory is named \"extcap\". The extcap man page says\n\n> When Wireshark launches an extcap, it automatically adds its installation path (normally C:\\Program Files\\Wireshark\\) to the DLL search path so that the extcap library dependencies can be found (it is not designed to be launched by hand).\n> This is done on purpose. There should only be extcap programs (executables, Python scripts, ...) in the extcap folder to reduce the startup time and not have Wireshark trying to execute other file types.\n\nExtcaps still work on my Windows VM with version 4.1.0rc0-1171, but I don't see anything in `extcap/*` that adjusts the DLL search path.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789801377",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-12-23T03:53:04.648Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-12-23T03:53:04.648Z",
